Rules in force for supply-chain-codex-chatgpt
File: codex-chatgpt.yaml
Note: Read from the file as written: it does not compile now, so nothing here says what a run enforces.

Can read: Files the agent can open and read.
  Can read any other file on this computer, except the ones under Never reads and Always on.

Can change: Files and folders the agent can create, edit or delete.
  - Can change files in ./src/  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ./tests/  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ./vendor/  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in ./tmp/  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change /dev/null  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change /dev/tty  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change /dev/ptmx  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in /dev/pts/  [line 33; editable]
  - Can change files in @@CODEXHOME@@/  [line 33; editable]
  Cannot change anything else.

Asks you first: The agent waits until you answer on the dashboard.
  - Asks you before it reads @@DENY_TOKEN@@  [line 37; editable]
  - Asks you before it reads files in ./confidential/  [line 37; editable]
  - Asks you before it changes files in ./held/  [line 38; editable]
  If you do not answer within 5 minutes, the answer is no.

Never reads: Files the agent can never open, whatever it tries.
  - Can never read @@DENY_SSH@@  [line 36; editable]

Programs: The programs the agent can start.
  - Can run codex, the command it starts with  [line 25]
  - Can run bash  [line 44; editable]
  - Can run git  [line 45; editable]
  - Can run env  [line 46; editable]
  - Can run sh  [line 47; editable]
