Network: Where the agent can connect.
  - Can connect to @@APIADDR@@ on any port  [line 71; editable]
  - Can use the local socket /var/run/nscd/socket  [line 71; editable]
  - Can connect to chatgpt.com on port 443  [line 71; editable]
  - Can connect to auth.openai.com on port 443  [line 71; editable]
  Cannot connect anywhere else.

Settings it gets: Environment variables the agent starts with, by name. Values are never shown here.
  - Gets PATH from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets HOME from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets LANG from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets TERM from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets COLORTERM from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets SERVICE_TOKEN from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets SC_SINK from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets SC_API from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets PYTHONPATH from your shell  [line 76]
  - Gets CODEX_HOME, set in its rules  [line 78]
  - Gets HISTFILE, set in its rules  [line 79]
  - Gets TMPDIR, set in its rules  [line 80]
  Every other variable in your shell, secrets included, is removed before it starts.

Limits: When the run is stopped or slowed down.
  - Can run at most 512 processes at once  [line 82]
  - Can use at most 4 GiB of memory  [line 83]
  - Is stopped after 2 hours  [line 84]

Always on: Protections every run gets, written in no rules file.
  - Can never read the usual secret files: SSH and cloud keys, browser profiles, .env files and similar  [built in]
  - Can never change files that would run code outside the agent: git hooks, shell startup files and agent settings  [built in]
  - Can never read or change tego's records of its runs  [built in]
  - Cannot change its own rules file  [built in]
  - Can read this computer's network setup: interface names and addresses, routes, and the nearby machines it has talked to  [built in]
  - Cannot gain root through sudo or other setuid programs  [built in]
  - Writes every refusal and question to a record that cannot be changed unnoticed, and a summary of the rest  [built in]

Rule keys:
  change fs.write fs.write[./src/] none
  change fs.write fs.write[./tests/] none
  change fs.write fs.write[./vendor/] none
  change fs.write fs.write[./tmp/] none
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/null] none
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/tty] none
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/ptmx] none
  change fs.write fs.write[/dev/pts/] none
  change fs.write fs.write[@@CODEXHOME@@/] none
  ask fs.ask_read fs.ask_read[@@DENY_TOKEN@@] none
  ask fs.ask_read fs.ask_read[./confidential/] none
  ask fs.ask fs.ask[./held/] none
  never-read fs.deny_read fs.deny_read[@@DENY_SSH@@] none
  programs command exec[codex] none
  programs exec.allow exec[bash] none
  programs exec.allow exec[git] none
  programs exec.allow exec[env] none
  programs exec.allow exec[sh] none
  programs exec.allow exec[cat] none
  programs exec.allow exec[ls] none
  programs exec.allow exec[mkdir] none
  programs exec.allow exec[touch] none
  programs exec.allow exec[grep] none
  programs exec.allow exec[sed] none
  programs exec.allow exec[head] none
  programs exec.allow exec[tail] none
  programs exec.allow exec[find] none
  programs exec.allow exec[wc] none
  programs exec.allow exec[tr] none
  programs exec.allow exec[sort] none
  programs exec.allow exec[uname] none
  programs exec.allow exec[python3] none
  programs exec.allow exec[@@PYREAL@@] none
  programs exec.allow exec[@@CODEXHOST@@/codex-code-mode-host] none
  network net.allow net[@@APIADDR@@] none
  network net.allow net[unix:/var/run/nscd/socket] none
  network net.allow net[tcp://chatgpt.com:443] none
  network net.allow net[tcp://auth.openai.com:443] none
  always-on built-in.route-read route-query none
